    title "What is the monkeypox virus? Basic information, Symptoms, diagnosis and Prevention. Science Today"
    description "There is always GREED for everything. The greed of science will increase as much as you gain. This is SCIENCE channel for those who willing to know out of syllabus. &#10;Here in this video you will find....Monkeypox &#10;it is a viral zoonosis (a virus transmitted to humans from animals) with symptoms very similar to those seen in the past in smallpox patients, although it is clinically less severe. &#10;Various animal species have been identified as susceptible to monkeypox virus. This includes rope squirrels, tree squirrels, Gambian pouched rats, dormice, non-human primates and other species. &#10;Uncertainty remains on the natural history of monkeypox virus and further studies are needed to identify the exact reservoir(s) and how virus circulation is maintained in nature.&#10;&#10;Keep watching, keep curious and keep learning new things."
