  [
    id 217
    label "mIAPIxBmGxs"
    step 0
    date "2022-05-23T13:30:58Z"
    title "Monkeypox virus MCQ #disease #CEC #mcq #currentaffairs #Sshom #virus #monkeypox"
    description "Answer: (c)&#10;&#10;Explanation:&#10;Monkeypox is a zoonotic disease. This means that the disease-causing organism originates in animals and jumps to humans. Monkeypox virus (MPV) is a double standard DNA virus. This virus is carried by animals including primates. It causes disease in both primates and in other animals. The virus is mainly found in tropical rainforest regions of Central and West Africa. &#10;&#10;The virus can spread both from animal to human and from human to human. If a person is bitten by an infected animal or the person comes in direct contact with the infected animal's bodily fluids, transmission from animal to human occurs. &#10;Transmission from human to human can occur by droplet respiration and contact with an infected person's bodily fluids.&#10;Hence, statement 3 is correct.&#10;&#10;Now let us look at the R-naught of the virus.&#10;The reproductive number of a virus or R0 denotes the number of people infected on an average by one infected person. If R0 is 2, then an infected person is expected to infect, on average, 2 other persons. Look at this diagram. Here the R0 is 2. This means that the patient zero infects 2 other persons. Further, these 2 persons will infect 2 other persons each, and the chain will continue like this.&#10;&#10;According to studies, the R0 of the monkeypox is relatively low (somewhere between 1 and 2). So, it is not as highly transmissible as measles, smallpox or COVID19.&#10;Hence, statement 2 is wrong.&#10;&#10;In COVID, infected people can spread the disease before developing symptoms. But monkeypox is not considered contagious before people develop symptoms, which makes it harder for people to unknowingly spread it. In places having better accessibility to supportive care, deaths due to monkeypox are rare.&#10;&#10;Monkeypox virus is related to smallpox and immunity to smallpox is protective against monkeypox. Treatments approved for smallpox could potentially be used to treat monkeypox infections. This is not a novel disease and we are equipped to manage the outbreak. Although monkeypox is not related to chickenpox, the characteristic monkeypox rash looks a lot like it. It starts as red spots on the mouth and face and then spreads to the arms and legs. &#10;Hence, statement 1 is correct.&#10;&#10;So our answer is (c). &#10;&#10;Source:&#10;https://www.vox.com/science-and-health/2022/5/19/23126248/monkeypox-infections-covid-outbreak-smallpox&#10;&#10;#UPSC #mcqs #prelims #upsc"
    channeltitle "Sshom "
