    title "MPV Monkeypox Virus LAMP Kit"
    description "Monkeypox Virus, a genus of orthopox viruses, can grow in the kidney cells of African green monkeys and cause cellular lesions.&#10;Monkeypox virus is a genus of orthopox viruses that can grow in the kidney cells of African green monkeys, causing cytopathic changes. Humans are infected with monkeypox mainly through the bite of an infected animal, or direct&#10;The infection of humans with monkeypox occurs mainly through bites from infected animals or direct contact with blood, body fluids, or monkeypox lesions of infected animals; it is usually transmitted from animals to humans, and occasionally can&#10;Occasionally, human-to-human transmission of monkeypox can occur. It is generally believed to be transmitted through direct, prolonged face-to-face contact with a&#10;Monkeypox is thought to be spread by a large number of respiratory droplets containing virus during direct, prolonged face-to-face contact. Monkeypox can also be transmitted through direct contact with infected body fluids or virus-contaminated&#10;Monkeypox can also be transmitted through direct contact with infected body fluids or items contaminated with the virus (e.g., clothing and bedding). The main clinical symptoms are fever, severe headache, swollen lymph nodes, back pain, and muscle pain (myalgia).&#10;The main clinical symptoms are fever, severe headache, swollen lymph nodes, back pain, muscular pain (muscle aches), and weakness (lack of energy). Therefore, rapid detection of monkeypox virus&#10;It is important to detect monkeypox virus quickly. This product is a kit for the detection of monkeypox virus based on the qPCR technique of the probe method.&#10;It has the following features: 1.&#10;1. ready to use, the user only needs to provide the sample DNA template. 2.&#10;The primers and probes are optimized for high analytical sensitivity up to 100 copies/&#956;L. 3.&#10;3. Positive controls are provided to facilitate the differentiation of false negative samples.&#10;4. High specificity, the primers are designed based on the highly conserved region of monkeypox virus DNA and will not cross-react with the DNA of other organisms.&#10;The primers are designed based on the highly conserved region of monkeypox DNA and will not cross-react with DNA of other organisms.&#10;5. Can be used for both qualitative and quantitative assays. The linear range for quantitative detection is at least 5&#10;The linear range is at least 5 orders of magnitude.&#10;6. The product is sufficient for 50 times of 20 &#956;L system of fluorescent quantitative PCR reactions with probes.&#10;7. This product can only be used for research."
