    title "Monkeypox Virus in Pakistan | Urdu-Hindi | Dr Waqar Rabbani"
    description "#Monkeypox #MonkeypoxVirus MonkeypoxPakistan #DrWaqarRabbani&#10;Information about monkeypox cases in Pakistan....&#10;Outbreak of monkey-pox in European countries &#10;According to the World Health Organization, the Monkey-pox virus has now spread to 12 countries including European countries, America, Canada and Australia etc. More than 100 cases have been reported. No case has been reported in Pakistan so far but there are chances that other countries of the world may be affected. It is an old virus that was discovered in a monkey around 1958, so it was named after a monkey. The first human case was reported in the 1970s in republic of the Congo.  The virus is commonly found in African countries. This is the first time that it has spread from Africa to other countries.&#10;&#10;Monkey pox virus is a rare disease that belongs to the family of chicken pox or small pox viruses, which has similar symptoms and usually lasts for a few weeks and it can not spread rapidly than other viruses. &#10;&#10;Monkey-pox is caused by a virus that is transmitted from animals to humans, symptoms are just like chicken pox or smallpox patients , flu including fever, body aches, headache, chills, weakness, restlessness, swollen lymph nodes, rashes begin on the face and spread on all over the body, palms and soles. Its symptoms is almost just like chicken pox or small pox but not severe like that.  The illness usually lasts for about two to four weeks.&#10;&#10;The virus, like other viruses, can enter the body or transmitted from human to human through respiratory tract,  infected broken skin, mouth, eyes, nose, sexual activity, or close contact with an infected patient, animal or contaminated material.&#10;&#10;According to the Centers for Disease Control and Prevention, there are no specific drugs or vaccines for the treatment of this virus, but the smallpox vaccine is very effective in this disease. So the smallpox vaccine or the use of antiviral drugs may be beneficial. As an alternative medicine in homeopathic medicine the same drugs will be useful and beneficial that are used in chicken pox or small pox such as Variolinum, Sulphur, Rhus tox, Antum. crud, Antum tart, Pulsatilla, Rananculus bulb, Merc sol, Thuja etc. Homeopathic remedies like Variolinum, Vaccinum, Malandrinum can also be used as a preventive.&#10;&#10;Dr. Waqar Rabbani &#10;northwesthmc@gmail.com&#10;@North West Homoeo Medical &#38; Research Centre"
