    title "What is Monkeypox virus?"
    description "What is Monkeypox virus?&#10;The monkeypox virus is a DNA virus with two strands that causes monkeypox in humans and other animals. It belongs to the family Poxviridae and the genus Orthopoxvirus. It's a type of human orthopoxvirus that also comprises variola, cowpox, and vaccinia."
