    title "The epidemic is growing! 10,000 people caught the monkeypox virus!"
    description "The World Health Organization (WHO) reported that the spread of the monkeypox virus continues around the world and the number of cases is approaching 10 thousand.&#10;WHO Director-General Dr. Tedros Adhanom Ghebreyesus evaluated the latest situation in the monkeypox epidemic at the press conference held at the organization's headquarters in Geneva.&#10;Ghebreyesus noted that they confirmed a total of 9,200 cases in 63 countries where the virus is endemic and non-endemic, and stated that there was no change in the number of deaths.&#10;Regarding the possibility of declaring an emergency due to the virus, Ghebreyesus said, &#34;The Emergency Committee will meet next week to evaluate the trend in monkeypox cases and the effectiveness of the methods of fighting the virus. Advice will be given on how countries should fight this epidemic.&#34;&#10;Emphasizing that WHO has started negotiations with the relevant countries regarding the development and distribution of vaccines against monkeypox, Ghebreyesus shared the information, &#34;As WHO, we continue to negotiate with various countries and experts to conduct further research on the epidemic.&#34;&#10;In its monkeypox report on July 7, WHO announced that 3 people have died so far due to the virus."
